window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>I'd spent my entire life voiceless.</b></p> <p>Ignored. Put to the side. All because I couldn't communicate with the humans that I was forced to be around. All because I wasn't surrounded by my kind. My parents subjected me to the worst type of loneliness because of their history—their hatred.</p> <p>My eighteenth birthday changed everything. Forever marked as the day that I decided to leave my sheltered existence and move to Willowdale Village…I just couldn't have expected what I would find there. Willowdale Village was a place that signified the exact opposite of my upbringing. A place where I found a potential best friend. A place where I began dreaming of opening up my own business—a cozy ballet studio. A place where I didn't have to worry about being judged because everyone was different and unique.</p> <p>A place where I met the three Graves brothers. Dominant, possessive, wolf shifters who planned on changing my life forever, making me think that maybe this village could be my new home.</p> <p>But what happens when my parents come to visit with an unexpected guest? One who not only wants to bring me back to where I grew up, but also place a very unwanted ring on my finger?</p> <p>I will have to find my voice if I want to keep my freedom.</p> <p>Voiceless <i>is book one in the Willowdale Village Collection, a paranormal romance reverse harem standalone for mature listeners. The</i> <i>Willowdale Village collection consists of several standalone stories about the women who live in this cozy supernatural town and their stories of finding themselves and love. You won't find any dark romance here, only possessive alpha males and true happily ever afters. Each woman is absolutely unique and strong for their own reason.</i></p>"; 
